From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:45:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Send the group key epoch past a device it cannot be encrypted
 for, and log the fan-out

Seen live: after a 1:1 call became a group call, one member's device never
received the new group key, so nobody could decrypt anybody and the call
timed out. The fan-out aborted as a whole when one recipient's key could not
be encrypted, before sending to anyone; now each recipient is encrypted and
sent independently and the failures are reported together.

The key exchange was only logged at debug level, which the integrator drops,
so a report could not tell who was nominated or who was sent the key. These
now log at info: a group invite and a group update with their transaction,
rekey nomination and roster counts; a group rekey received (from whom) and
installed; and every distribution with its recipients, how many were sent
and failed, and the connected devices skipped for having no PID.

Tested: the fan-out goes on past a device that cannot be encrypted and
addresses each node to its own recipient; connected devices without a PID are
named; full suite passes.
